# -------------------------------
# Git Ignore File for AI-Resume-Analyzer
# it tells Docker which files/folders to ignore/Exclude when building images.
# That keeps your Docker image clean and smaller.
# Prevents copying unnecessary files (Git history, caches, IDE configs, test outputs).
# Ensures only source code + required files go into the container.
# -------------------------------

# Git   
# Don't copy GIT's Internal folders into Docker Image.
.git
.github

# Virtual environments
# Don't copy Python virtual environments and environment files  into Docker Image. 
# (they contain secrets and dependencies, not needed inside the image).
.venv
.env
.env.*

# Python cache and compiled files
# Don't copy Python’s auto‑generated cache and compiled files  into Docker Image.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# Testing and coverage outputs
# Don't copy test results, lint/type‑check caches, and coverage reports into Docker Image.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# IDE/editor settings
# Exclude IDE project settings (PyCharm, VS Code).
.idea/
.vscode/

# Project-specific ignores
# Skip uv.lock (dependency lock file) and optionally tests/ if you don’t want test code inside the Docker image.

uv.lock   # Lock file generated by uv package manager
tests/    # Test files (optional to ignore if not needed in repo)